While it is certainly possible for someone to sue the Dev team, I
don't think they'd stand a very good chance of winning.  Why?

1) nethack isn't commercial.
2) The only thing taken from these books is mere names: in other
words, any copying that occurred was minimal.

thus, the use of these names probably falls under the "fair use"
exception to the copyright act.

And even before we get to the fair use analysis, I don't think enough
expression was copied from the copyrighted works to support a suit.
Now, if whole chapters or paragraphs had been taken, that's another
story.

